<title>BELGIUM: EU sugar panel to review levy data.</title>
<headline>EU sugar panel to review levy data.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar management committee on Wednesday will review production and consumption statistics for the marketing years 1991-95, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The review of data to establish whether any changes in consumption have been identified since the figures were submitted by member states is preparatory to fixing new production levies,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>A European Commission official added that production levies, which finance export refunds, could be set by the committee as early as September 18 or, at the latest by September 25.</p>
<p>&quot;The levies must be fixed by October 15 in order that member states can ensure that they are paid by December 15. On Wednesday we will be reviewing the basic data,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom: +32 2 287-6830</p>
</text>
